---
import SubpageLayout from '../../layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';
import transportData from '../../data/transport.json';

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'How do I get to Nauru?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Nauru Airlines operates flights from Brisbane (4 hours) and Nadi/Fiji (3 hours). There are no passenger ferries or cruise ships. Nauru International Airport (INU) has a single runway and compact terminal.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'How do I get around Nauru?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Car rental ($50–80 AUD/day) is the best option. There is no public transport. The island is 19 km around — walking takes 4–5 hours. Bicycles are available at some hotels. Taxis exist but are ad-hoc with no formal ranks or booking apps.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'What do I need to rent a car in Nauru?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Your home country driving licence is valid for short-term visits (up to 3 months). Minimum age is typically 21–25. A cash deposit or credit card pre-authorisation is usually required. Fuel is available at the Nauru Fuel Station in Aiwo.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'How do I get from the airport to my accommodation?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Arrange hotel pickup before departure. Taxis are available outside the terminal but pre-booked hotel transfers are recommended. Store airport and accommodation contact details offline before you travel.',
      },
    },
  ],
};
---

<SubpageLayout title={transportData.title} description={transportData.subtitle} sectionEmoji="🚢" sectionLabel="Getting Around" includeTopBar={true} includeFooter={true}>

  <img src="/assets/images/nauru_transport_00001_.png" alt="Nauru International Airport with airplane on runway" class="hero-image" style="width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin-bottom:2rem">
  <Fragment slot="jsonld">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema, null, 2)} />
  </Fragment>
  <p>{transportData.intro}</p>

  <div class="callout-grid">
    <div class="callout"><h3>✈️ Fly in, fly out</h3><p>Nauru Airlines operates flights from Brisbane (4 hrs) and Nadi/Fiji (3 hrs). No passenger ferries or cruise ships call here.</p></div>
    <div class="callout"><h3>🚗 Rent a car</h3><p>No public transport. Car hire ($50–80 AUD/day) is the best way to explore. Drive on the left — Australian system.</p></div>
    <div class="callout"><h3>🌴 Island is 19 km around</h3><p>The ring road circles the entire island. Walking takes 4–5 hours. Bicycles available at some hotels — perfect for exploring.</p></div>
    <div class="callout"><h3>⚠️ Plan before arrival</h3><p>No ride-hailing apps, no taxi dispatch. Arrange airport pickup or car hire in advance through your hotel.</p></div>
  </div>

  {transportData.sections.map((s) => (
    <Fragment>
      <h2>{s.heading}</h2>
      {s.content.split('\n\n').map((p) => (p.trim() ? <p>{p}</p> : null))}
    </Fragment>
  ))}

  <h2>✈️ Nauru Airlines Flight Schedule</h2>
  <p>Nauru Airlines (formerly Our Airline) is the only commercial carrier serving Nauru International Airport (INU). The airline operates a Boeing 737-700/800 on its regular routes. Below is a summary of current connections — <strong>always verify directly with Nauru Airlines</strong> as schedules change frequently.</p>

  <div class="listings-block">
    <div class="route-card">
      <h3>🇦🇺 Brisbane (BNE) → Nauru (INU)</h3>
      <div class="route-details">
        <div class="rd"><strong>Duration:</strong> ~4 hours</div>
        <div class="rd"><strong>Frequency:</strong> 2–3 flights per week</div>
        <div class="rd"><strong>Aircraft:</strong> Boeing 737-700/800</div>
        <div class="rd"><strong>Notes:</strong> Main gateway — most visitors arrive via Brisbane. Baggage allowance and meal service vary by fare class.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <h3>🇫🇯 Nadi (NAN) → Nauru (INU)</h3>
      <div class="route-details">
        <div class="rd"><strong>Duration:</strong> ~3 hours</div>
        <div class="rd"><strong>Frequency:</strong> 1–2 flights per week (less frequent than Brisbane)</div>
        <div class="rd"><strong>Aircraft:</strong> Boeing 737-700/800</div>
        <div class="rd"><strong>Notes:</strong> Alternative entry point connecting from Pacific routes. Useful for travellers coming from Asia or New Zealand via Fiji.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="info-box">
    <h4>🛬 Nauru International Airport (INU) — What to Expect</h4>
    <p>The airport has a single runway and a compact terminal. There are no jet bridges — you walk across the tarmac. Immigration is straightforward but queues can form when multiple flights arrive simultaneously. The small departures lounge has basic seating and a duty-free shop selling souvenirs, alcohol, and tobacco. No café or restaurant is available airside — bring snacks if needed. Luggage retrieval is manual, so be patient. On departure, arrive at least 2 hours early — check-in and security are slow-paced.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>🚗 Car Rental in Detail</h2>
  <p>With no public transport system, a rental car gives you freedom to explore the island at your own pace. Here is what you need to know:</p>

  <div class="rental-card">
    <h3>Rental Requirements</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Driving licence:</strong> Your home country licence is valid for short-term visits (up to 3 months).</li>
      <li><strong>Age:</strong> Minimum age is typically 21–25 (varies by provider; check in advance).</li>
      <li><strong>Deposit:</strong> A cash deposit or credit card pre-authorisation is usually required.</li>
      <li><strong>Fuel:</strong> Petrol is available at the Nauru Fuel Station in Aiwo. Hours are limited — fill up when you see it open.</li>
      <li><strong>Insurance:</strong> Basic insurance is included in most rentals; check for excess amounts.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="rental-card">
    <h3>Estimated Costs</h3>
    <div class="cost-grid">
      <div class="cost-item"><span>Economy sedan (per day)</span> <strong>$50–$65 AUD</strong></div>
      <div class="cost-item"><span>SUV / 4WD (per day)</span> <strong>$70–$90 AUD</strong></div>
      <div class="cost-item"><span>Weekly discount (estimated)</span> <strong>~10–15% off daily rate</strong></div>
      <div class="cost-item"><span>Fuel (per litre)</span> <strong>~$1.80–$2.20 AUD</strong></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>🚕 Other Transport Options</h2>
  <div class="transport-options">
    <div class="option-card">
      <h3>🚶 Walking</h3>
      <p>The island is small enough to explore on foot, especially the Yaren and Aiwo districts. The coastal ring road is flat and walkable. A full circuit is about 19 km (4–5 hours). Bring water, sun protection, and sturdy shoes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="option-card">
      <h3>🚲 Bicycles</h3>
      <p>Some hotels (Menen Hotel, OD-N-Aiwo) offer bicycle hire for guests. Cycling is an excellent way to cover ground at a leisurely pace. Roads are flat but watch for loose dogs and potholes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="option-card">
      <h3>🚕 Taxis</h3>
      <p>Taxi services exist but are ad-hoc — no formal ranks or booking apps. Ask your hotel to arrange one. Fares should be agreed in advance. Expect $10–$20 AUD for most intra-island trips.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>✅ Transport Checklist</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Confirm your arrival flight and arrange hotel pickup <strong>before departure</strong>.</li>
    <li>Store airport and accommodation contact details <strong>offline</strong>.</li>
    <li>If renting a car, arrange it before arrival — availability is limited.</li>
    <li>Keep AUD cash for fuel (cards rarely accepted at petrol stations).</li>
    <li>Download offline maps (Google Maps or Maps.me) — mobile data is slow.</li>
    <li>Be cautious driving at night — limited street lighting and animals on roads.</li>
    <li>Speed limits: 40 km/h in built-up areas, 60 km/h on open roads. No traffic lights anywhere on the island.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Next steps</h2>
  <div class="utility-grid">
    <a href="/visit/visa/" class="utility-card"><h3>🛂 Visa requirements</h3><p>Make sure your documents are in order.</p></a>
    <a href="/visit/accommodation/" class="utility-card"><h3>🏨 Accommodation guide</h3><p>Find a place to stay near the airport.</p></a>
    <a href="/visit/currency/" class="utility-card"><h3>💵 Currency & payments</h3><p>Cash for fuel and transport costs.</p></a>
    <a href="/visit/" class="utility-card"><h3>🗺️ Visit hub</h3><p>Back to the main travel guide.</p></a>
  </div>
</SubpageLayout>

<style>
  .callout-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px;margin:1.5rem 0}
  .callout{background:#fff;border:2px solid #1a1a2e;padding:18px;box-shadow:4px 4px 0 #1a1a2e}
  .callout h3{margin:0 0 8px;font-family:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;color:#002B7F}
  @media (max-width: 720px){.callout-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}

  .listings-block{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;margin:1.5rem 0}
  .route-card{background:#fff;border:2px solid #1a1a2e;padding:20px;box-shadow:4px 4px 0 #1a1a2e}
  .route-card h3{margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;color:#002B7F;font-size:1.1rem}
  .route-details{display:grid;gap:6px}
  .rd{font-size:14px;color:#475569;line-height:1.6}
  .rd strong{color:#1a1a2e}

  .rental-card{background:#fff;border:2px solid #1a1a2e;padding:20px;margin:1rem 0;box-shadow:4px 4px 0 #1a1a2e}
  .rental-card h3{margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;color:#002B7F}
  .rental-card ul{margin:0;list-style:none;padding:0}
  .rental-card ul li{font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#475569;padding:4px 0;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative}
  .rental-card ul li::before{content:'•';position:absolute;left:0;color:#FFC72C;font-weight:bold}

  .cost-grid{display:grid;gap:8px}
  .cost-item{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:14px;color:#475569;padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.06)}
  .cost-item:last-child{border-bottom:none}
  .cost-item strong{color:#1a1a2e}

  .transport-options{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px;margin:1.5rem 0}
  .option-card{background:#fff;border:2px solid #1a1a2e;padding:18px;box-shadow:4px 4px 0 #1a1a2e}
  .option-card h3{margin:0 0 8px;font-family:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;color:#002B7F;font-size:1rem}
  .option-card p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.7;color:#64748b;margin:0}
  @media (max-width: 720px){.transport-options{grid-template-columns:1fr}}

  h2 code{font-family:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;font-size:0.9rem;background:#f0f0f0;padding:2px 8px}
</style>
